port sysutils/conmon
type port
reason "DragonFly: take conmon's FreeBSD paths, binding the attach socket without bindat() (dragonfly/@<line> patches)"

# conmon's BSD code is keyed on __FreeBSD__ (ECOMM, procctl reaper and
# pdeathsig, kqueue signal descriptor, /dev/fd, attach sockets), so on
# DragonFly cmsg.c stopped at an undeclared ECOMM and the rest would have
# fallen through to Linux-only code. Add __DragonFly__; DragonFly has no
# bindat(), so bind the socket name from inside the directory instead.
